3-methoxy-5-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)pyridine (2.05
g, 8.73 mmol) were dissolved in DME (60 mL) and the reaction flushed with
nitrogen for 10 minutes. Pd(dppf)Cl2 (713 mg, 0.873 mmol) was added and
the reaction flushed again with nitrogen for 10 minutes. Sodium carbonate
(2M, 17.5 mL, 35 mmol) was added and the reaction was stirred under
nitrogen at 90 °C for 2 h. Additional Pd(dppf)Cl2 (713 mg, 0.873 mmol)
was added and the reaction stirred at 100 °C overnight. The reaction
mixture was filtered through a plug of Florisil®, with the aid of EtOAc.
The filtrate was concentrated to a minimum volume in vacuo and the
addition of DCM/ether. 6-(5-methoxypyridin-3-yl)benzo[d]thiazol-2-amine
28 (2.239 g, 99.7%) as a brown solid that was collected by filtration and
dried in vacuo at 50 °C. 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ 8.62 (s, 1H), 8.38
(s, 1H), 8.20 (d, J = 1.7 Hz, 1H), 8.10 (br s, 2H), 7.90 (t, J = 1.7 Hz,
1H), 7.71 (dd, J = 2.1 Hz, 8.5 Hz, 1H), 7.47 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 1H), 3.97
(s, 3H); ESMS m/z 258.0 (M+ + 1).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling, incremental addition of
dichloro(diphenylphosphinoferrocene)palladium
