$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the isolation experiments. Into a degassed
supension of the pre-swelled gel catalyst PdGel (25:1) (50 mg) in the 80%
aq EtOH (50 °C, 20 mL) under Ar atmosphere for 1 h, the arylboronic acid
(3 mmol), potassium carbonate (6 mmol) and iodo- or bromoarene (2 mmol)
were added. The reaction mixture was heated to 50 °C (or 80 °C in the
case of bromoarenes) under Ar atmosphere (GC/MS monitoring). The reaction
was quenched with 5% aq HCl, extracted with ether, the organic layer was
dried by magnesium sulfate overnight, then after filtration the solution
was evaporated. The crude product was recrystallized from 20-40% aq EtOH
and dried. 1,1'-Biphenyl (a). 0.283 g (1.84 mmol; 92%) from bromobenzene;
white crystalline substance. M.p. 68.1-69.1 °C (Ref.1 68-69 °C).
Elemental analysis: For C12H10 (154.21) calculated (%): C 93.46; H 6.54;
found: C 93.34; H 6.49. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): 7.61 (d, J = 7.1, 4H,
H-2), 7.46 (t, J =7.5, 4H, H-3), 7.36 (t, J = 7.4, 2H, H-4). 13C NMR (101
MHz, CDCl3): 141.71, 129.21, 127.70, 127.63.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative preparation shown, GC yield, 92% isolated yield, palladium
embedded in cross-linked polyhydromethylsiloxane gel prepared and used as
catalyst, Suzuki-Miyaura cross-coupling reaction
